Comment (cmd/seed/workflows.go:493):
Using `clause.OnConflict{UpdateAll: true}` will update *every* column on re-import, including `created_at`, `deleted_at` (potentially undeleting soft-deleted records), and audit fields like `created_by_id`/`updated_by_id` (which are unset in the seed structs and would be overwritten to NULL). This can unintentionally destroy audit history and resurrect deleted data. Prefer an explicit `DoUpdates` column allowlist per model type so only intended business fields are updated on conflict.
Implementation guidance: In cmd/seed/workflows.go, replace the generic clause.OnConflict{UpdateAll: true} in upsertWorkflowSeed with an explicit DoUpdates allowlist chosen by model type. Keep the existing primary-key existence count and Create-with-OnConflict flow, but do not update id, created_at, deleted_at, created_by_id, updated_by_id, or relationship/computed fields. For *workflows.WorkflowDefinition update only name, description, version, suggested_cadence, evidence_required, grace_period_days, and updated_at. For *workflows.WorkflowStepDefinition update workflow_definition_id, name, description, order, responsible_role, evidence_required, estimated_duration, grace_period_days, and updated_at. For *workflows.ControlRelationship update workflow_definition_id, control_id, control_source, catalog_id, relationship_type, strength, is_active, and updated_at. For *workflows.WorkflowInstance update workflow_definition_id, name, description, system_security_plan_id, cadence, is_active, grace_period_days, next_scheduled_at, last_executed_at, and updated_at; preserveWorkflowInstanceSchedule should continue to populate the scheduling fields before this upsert so re-imports do not move existing schedules. For *workflows.RoleAssignment update workflow_instance_id, role_name, assigned_to_type, assigned_to_id, and is_active; it has no timestamps or audit fields. A clean approach is to add a helper like workflowSeedUpdateColumns(value interface{}) ([]string, error) and call clause.OnConflict{Columns: []clause.Column{{Name: "id"}}, DoUpdates: clause.AssignmentColumns(columns)}. Keep workflowSeedID or combine its type switch carefully, and return an unsupported-type error for unknown models. Add or update focused tests in cmd/seed/workflows_test.go that seed an existing soft-deleted/audited workflow definition or workflow instance with CreatedByID/UpdatedByID/DeletedAt set, re-import the same deterministic seed row, and assert the intended business fields update while DeletedAt and audit fields are not cleared or overwritten.
